 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nRelationship type comparison fails with mixed case\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen working with documents that have relationship types with mixed case (e.g., \"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/Image\" vs \"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officedocument/2006/relationships/image\"), the relationship type matching fails unexpectedly.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\n# Load a document with images or other relationships\ndocument = Document('document_with_images.docx')\n\n# Try to iterate through content - this may fail silently or produce unexpected results\nfor item in document.iter_inner_content():\n    print(type(item))\n\n# Or try accessing image parts\npackage = document.part.package\nimage_parts = package.image_parts\nprint(f\"Found {len(image_parts)} image parts\")  # May show 0 when images exist\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when the document contains relationship types that don't match the expected case exactly. For example, if a document has relationship types like \"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/Image\" (with mixed case), but the code expects \"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officedocument/2006/relationships/image\" (all lowercase), the matching will fail.\n\nThis can result in:\n- Missing content when iterating through document elements\n- Image parts not being detected properly\n- Inconsistent behavior depending on how the original document was created\n</issue>\n",
